   "scion_answer": "To find $\\frac{-5}{9} \\cdot \\frac{8}{17}$, we multiply the numerators and denominators:\n\n$$\\frac{-5}{9} \\cdot \\frac{8}{17} = \\frac{-5 \\cdot 8}{9 \\cdot 17} = \\frac{-40}{153}$$\n\nSince 40 and 153 share no common factors (40 = 2\u00b2 \u00d7 5 and 153 = 3\u00b2 \u00d7 17), the fraction is in simplest form.\n\n$$\\boxed{\\dfrac{-40}{153}}$$",
