  {
   "id": "math-0013",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "The decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$ is $0.142857142857\\dots$, which has a repeating period of length 6: $\\{1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7\\}$.\n\nSince the period is 6, the $n$-th digit corresponds to the $(n \\mod 6)$-th position in the repeating sequence (with $n=0$ giving the first digit).\n\nWe compute:\n$$2007 \\mod 6 = 2007 - 6 \\cdot 334 = 2007 - 2004 = 3$$\n\nThe 3rd digit in the sequence $\\{1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7\\}$ is **2**.\n\n$$\\boxed{2}$$",
