   "id": "humaneval-0015",
   "bucket": "code",
   "planned_path": "P4",
   "scion_answer": "```python\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Algorithm idea is simple:\n    - Find the longest postfix of supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    - Append to the end of the string reverse of a string prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix.\n    >>> make_palindrome('')\n    ''\n    >>> make_palindrome('cat')\n    'catac'\n    >>> make_palindrome('cata')\n    'catac'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return ''\n    \n    # Find the longest palindrome postfix\n    n = len(string)\n    longest_palindrome_suffix = ''\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Check if string[i:] is a palindrome\n        if string[i:] == string[i:][::-1]:\n            longest_palindrome_suffix = string[i:]\n            break\n    \n    # The prefix before the palindrome suffix\n    prefix = string[:n - len(longest_palindrome_suffix)]\n    \n    # Reverse the prefix and append to the end\n    return string + prefix[::-1]\n```",
